<title>UK: British Gas says MMC won't delay demerger.</title>
<headline>British Gas says MMC won't delay demerger.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Gas Plc's decision to reject price controls on its TransCo gas transmission business will not affect the company's plans for a demerger next year, deputy chairman Philip Rogerson said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In a telephone interview with Reuters, Rogerson said the decision on the price controls &quot;does not create any uncertainty about the business to be demerged,&quot; which is British Gas's domestic supply business, British Gas Energy.</p>
<p>He said plans for the demerger are still on track for the spring of next year.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
